ps: Display information about active processes.(Just your processes in the current terminal)

ps -ef: Display detailed information about all processes.
        -e → show every process on the system (not just yours)
        -f → full format (more columns/detail — like PPID, start time)

kill process_id: Terminate a process with the specified process ID.

killall process_name: Terminate all processes with the specified name.

top: Display real-time information about system processes.

bg: Put a process in the background.

fg: Bring a background process to the foreground.

nproc: prints the number of processing units (CPU cores) available to the current process.
